{
  "id": "fence_posts",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Fence Posts",
  "world": "world_01",
  "chapter": "count_marks_inclusive_end",
  "tier": 1,
  "mode": "repair",
  "concepts": [
    "variables",
    "control"
  ],
  "prerequisites": [],
  "story": "A fence runs along a field edge that is some metres long. A post stands at 0 metres, and then one every gap metres for as long as it is still on the fence; a post exactly at the far end counts too. The program should count the posts, but sometimes its answer is one short. Find the mistake and fix it.",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {
        "name": "length",
        "type": "num"
      },
      {
        "name": "gap",
        "type": "num"
      }
    ],
    "output": {
      "type": "num"
    }
  },
  "constraints": {
    "notes": [
      "The fence is 0 to 500 metres long.",
      "The gap is a whole number from 1 to 50."
    ]
  },
  "blocks": {
    "allow": [
      "arith.add",
      "cmp.le",
      "cmp.lt",
      "ctrl.return",
      "ctrl.while",
      "lit.num",
      "var.get",
      "var.inc",
      "var.set"
    ],
    "maxBlocks": 23
  },
  "limits": {
    "maxOps": 2800,
    "maxDepth": 32,
    "maxAlloc": 50
  },
  "hints": [
    "Compare the two cases you can see: the answer is wrong only when a post lands exactly on the end of the fence.",
    "Follow pos through the loop for a 12 metre fence with a gap of 4. What happens when pos reaches 12?",
    "The WHILE condition stops one post early: the post at the very end needs LESS OR EQUAL, not LESS THAN."
  ],
  "validators": {
    "output": "equal"
  },
